---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import LegalPage from "../../components/LegalPage.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — HEART&SOUL" description="Privacy policy for HEART&SOUL, a brand of BHS tabletop AG.">
  <Header />
  <main>
    <LegalPage eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy Policy">
      <p>
        Thank you for your interest in HEART&amp;SOUL. Protecting your personal data is important to us. This
        website can generally be used without providing personal data. Where personal data is processed on this
        site, this is done in accordance with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and applicable
        German data protection law.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Controller</h2>
      <p>The controller within the meaning of the GDPR is:</p>
      <p>
        <strong>BHS tabletop AG</strong><br />
        Ludwigsmühle 1<br />
        95100 Selb<br />
        Germany<br />
        Phone: +49 9287 73-0<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:kontakt@bhs-tabletop.de">kontakt@bhs-tabletop.de</a>
      </p>

      <h2>2. Data Protection Officer</h2>
      <p>
        You can reach our data protection officer at:<br />
        BHS tabletop AG, Data Protection Officer, Ludwigsmühle 1, 95100 Selb, Germany<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:datenschutzbeauftragter@bhs-tabletop.de">datenschutzbeauftragter@bhs-tabletop.de</a>
      </p>

      <h2>3. Server log files</h2>
      <p>
        Each time this website is accessed, our hosting provider automatically collects general data and
        information (e.g. browser type, operating system, referrer URL, pages visited, date and time of access,
        and a shortened IP address). This data is used to ensure the technically error-free delivery and
        security of the website and does not allow conclusions to be drawn about your identity.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website uses cookies. Strictly necessary cookies are required for the website to function and are
        set without separate consent. In addition, we use — only with your consent — statistics cookies to
        analyze how the website is used. You can change or withdraw your choice at any time via the cookie
        banner at the bottom of the screen, or via the "Cookie settings" link in the footer of this website.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Google Analytics via Google Tag Manager</h2>
      <p>
        If you have given your consent, we use Google Tag Manager to embed the web analytics service Google
        Analytics, provided by Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland ("Google").
        Google Analytics uses cookies or comparable technologies that enable an analysis of how you use this
        website (e.g. pages visited, time spent, approximate location, technical device information).
      </p>
      <p>
        This processing takes place exclusively on the basis of your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR), which you give
        via the cookie banner. No analytics cookie is set and no usage data is transmitted to Google before you
        consent — this is technically enforced via "Google Consent Mode", which blocks data collection until you
        grant consent. You can withdraw your consent at any time with effect for the future by selecting
        "Necessary only" via the "Cookie settings" link in the footer.
      </p>
      <p>
        For more information on Google Analytics and data protection at Google, please visit
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Contacting us</h2>
      <p>
        If you contact us by email, the data you provide (e.g. name, email address, message) will be stored
        exclusively to process your inquiry and will not be shared with third parties without your consent.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>As a data subject, you have the following rights under the GDPR, in particular:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Right of access to your stored personal data (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
        <li>Right to rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
        <li>Right to erasure ("right to be forgotten", Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
        <li>Right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
        <li>Right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
        <li>Right to object to processing (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
        <li>Right to withdraw consent already given, with effect for the future (Art. 7(3) GDPR)</li>
        <li>Right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise these rights, please contact our Data Protection Officer (see section 2).</p>

      <h2>8. Data security</h2>
      <p>
        For security reasons, this website uses SSL/TLS encryption to protect the transmission of confidential
        content. You can recognize an encrypted connection by the "https://" in your browser's address bar.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to this privacy policy</h2>
      <p>
        We will update this privacy policy whenever the legal requirements or the functionality of this website
        change. The version currently published on this page always applies.
      </p>
    </LegalPage>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
